<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Q2 investments rise 13.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Hungary Q2 investments rise 13.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's investment volume rose 13.4 percent in the second quarter of 1997 in year-on-year terms, compared with 3.6 percent in the first quarter of this year, the Central Statistical Office said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>INVESTMENTS IN BRANCHES OF THE ECONOMY IN Q2</p>
<p>					 Nominal	    Volume</p>
<p>				    (bln forints)    (yr/yr pct change)</p>
<p>Agriculture, forestry,</p>
<p>   fishing				14.9	     +38,6</p>
<p> Mining				    1.2		+4.7</p>
<p> Processing industry		  86.9	     +24.6</p>
<p>Electricity-, gas-, water- distribution, district   heating				 23.1		+5.1</p>
<p> Construction industry		 7.7	     -24.6</p>
<p> Trade, maintenance services	15.6		-9.6</p>
<p> Hotel and catering		    2.8	     +33.9</p>
<p>Transport, post, telecommunications,   warehousing			   53.6	     +25.4</p>
<p> Financial services		    8.8	     +12.2</p>
<p>Real estate, leasing,   business support services	 81.1		+5.9</p>
<p>Public administration,   social security		     10.7	     +27.3</p>
<p> Education				 6.2	     +10.8</p>
<p> Health and social care		8.6	     +16.9</p>
<p>Other social, communal   or personal services		12.2	    +19.4</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------  TOTAL				   333.2	    +13.4</p>
<p>MATERIAL COMPOSITION OF INVESTMENTS</p>
<p>			 Nominal		 Volume</p>
<p>			(Forints)	   (yr/yr pct change)</p>
<p> Buildings	    160.5		   +1.7</p>
<p> Machinery	    144.7		  +32.7</p>
<p>  -Imported	    56.7		  +15.8</p>
<p>  -Domestic	    88.0		  +45.7</p>
<p> Other		   28.0		   +1.1</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------  TOTAL</p>
<p>		 333.2		  +13.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Second-quarter figures showed a further improvement in investment, but a relatively low base in the same period of 1996 must also be taken into account, the statistical office said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
